1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.
Genesis 1:1 (KJV)

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp.
Psalm 150:3 (KJV)

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:25,000
And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.
Genesis 1:2 (KJV)

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:25,000
And it came to pass, when the evil spirit from God was upon Saul, that David took an harp, and played with his hand: so Saul was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him.
1 Samuel 16:23 (KJV)

5
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:25,000
And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.
Genesis 1:3 (KJV)

6
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:25,000
Praise the LORD with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery and an instrument of ten strings.
Psalm 33:2 (KJV)

7
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:25,000
By the word of the LORD were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.
Psalm 33:6 (KJV)

8
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:25,000
The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.
Psalm 19:1 (KJV)

9
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:25,000
The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want. He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.
Psalm 23:1-2 (KJV)

10
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:25,000
Awake up, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I myself will awake early.
Psalm 57:8 (KJV)

11
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:25,000
Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.
Psalm 46:10 (KJV)

12
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:25,000
Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? there is no searching of his understanding.
Isaiah 40:28 (KJV)

13
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:25,000
Sing unto the LORD with the harp; with the harp, and the voice of a psalm.
Psalm 98:5 (KJV)

14
01:58:00,000 --> 01:58:25,000
I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.
Psalm 121:1-2 (KJV)

15
02:07:00,000 --> 02:07:25,000
Through faith we understand that the worlds were framed by the word of God, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear.
Hebrews 11:3 (KJV)

16
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:25,000
In his hand are the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills is his also. The sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land.
Psalm 95:4-5 (KJV)

17
02:25:00,000 --> 02:25:25,000
Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea, upon the harp will I praise thee, O God my God.
Psalm 43:4 (KJV)

18
02:34:00,000 --> 02:34:25,000
I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.
Psalm 139:14 (KJV)

19
02:43:00,000 --> 02:43:25,000
Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy pleasure they are and were created.
Revelation 4:11 (KJV)

20
02:52:00,000 --> 02:52:25,000
Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.
Psalm 16:11 (KJV)

